1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:09,800
Binnacle Connect: a companion app for tow-sport boats.
Pairing · live telemetry and video · recorded clips

2
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:14,600
The QR label on the device carries no secret.
Pairing also needs a window opened on the unit.

3
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:19,000
The key is generated on the phone. The private half
stays in secure storage; only the public key is sent.

4
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:28,000
A unit that reports no previous owner gets an explicit
warning instead of being claimed silently.

5
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:34,800
The warning has to be ticked before you can continue.

6
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:43,400
Device state, commands and acknowledgments travel on
an authenticated WebSocket control channel.

7
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:51,600
Video and HUD telemetry run on a separate WebRTC channel.
A stalled stream can never delay a safety acknowledgment.

8
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:59,800
The device is the source of truth: a command stays
pending until the device sends back new state.

9
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:09,800
Clip library: highlights, snapshots and safety clips,
with filters and favourites.

10
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:19,800
Saved highlights play back in the app.
Demo media is labelled as demo.

11
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:29,600
30 test suites in the app, plus database tests.
CI runs the checks on every change.
